.TH MYGREP 3 "September 2026" "libmyutils 0.4.1" "libmyutils Manual"
.SH NAME
mygrep \- find lines in a file that contain a string
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include "myfilefunctions.h"
.PP
.BI "int mygrep(FILE *" fp ", const char *" search_str ", char ***" matches ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mygrep()
reads the open file stream
.I fp
line by line and finds every line that contains
.IR search_str .
It allocates a list of copies of the matching lines and stores its
address in
.IR *matches .
The caller must free each line and then the list itself with
.BR free (3).
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the number of matching lines, or \-1 on failure.
